The fast match is over.
We walk off the court together.
I am very tired.
Kasper and Sara are also tired.
We drink some water.
"You play very well," Sara says.
"Thank you very much," I say.
"I think it is so much fun."
"Do you play often?" Kasper asks.
"Yes, I play a lot back home in Mexico," I answer.
"I usually play with my sister."
"It is a fun sport," Sara says.
"We love to play here in the club."
"I want to play more here in Denmark," I say.
"You are definitely fast," Kasper laughs.
"Thanks, but now I want to sit down," I say.
"Shall we go into the cafeteria?" Kasper asks.
"Yes, I would very much like that," I answer.
